{
 "id": "rewrite/searchfold-inside-prefix/hot/5m",
 "description": "A warm request (40 seconds after the last). searchfold shortens message 10, a 3,000-token output inside the cached prefix, to 500 tokens. The client breakpoints are the end of system, message 9 and the last message, so the provider reads through message 9 (33,000 tokens) and writes the other 16,500. searchfold saves 2,500 x $0.30 = +$0.00075 and breaks the cache on 14,500 tokens, 14,500 x ($3.75 - $0.30) = -$0.05003: net -$0.04928. The break carries searchfold's ChangeID, so the cost is visible where the dashboard in issue 496 showed a hit.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#496",
 "dims": {
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "position": "beforeBStar",
  "cache": "break",
  "ttl": "5m",
  "lifetime": "exact",
  "break": "plugin"
 },
 "rates": "fixture-v1",
 "open": [
  "design \u00a75.1 snaps B* to the last client breakpoint at or before the previous body's end, and the client's breakpoints are the current request's own: system and the new last message. Read literally that gives the end of system, not the end of the previous body. The examples, and this case, take the end of the previous body."
 ],
